# Ghana AI Innovation Challenge

An action research challenge for data scientists, technologists, researchers, and innovators to develop AI-powered solutions using Ghanaian datasets. Organised by [Ghana AI Summit](https://ghanaaisummit.com/), [Knowledge Innovations](https://knowledgeinnovations.com/), [Ghana AI Research Network (GAIN)](https://ghanaai.org) and partners.

## Objectives

What we aim to achieve

This action research challenge invites data scientists, technologists, researchers, and innovators to develop AI-powered tools and solutions using Ghanaian datasets. The challenge aims to:

*   Harness collective innovation to address local challenges using AI
*   Foster collaboration between technologists, domain experts, and practitioners
*   Generate actionable insights from Ghanaian data sources
*   Showcase the potential of AI to solve pressing problems in the Ghanaian context

## Problem Domains

Choose your focus area

Participants may develop solutions in any of the following domains:

#### Agriculture

Crop yield prediction, pest detection, market access, supply chain optimization

#### Healthcare

Disease detection, patient triage, diagnostic support, resource allocation

#### Financial Inclusion

Credit scoring, fraud detection, mobile money analytics, risk assessment

#### Public Services

Traffic management, service delivery optimization, urban planning, waste management

#### Education

Learning analytics, student performance prediction, personalized learning, resource allocation

**Note:** Solutions addressing challenges outside these domains may also be considered if they demonstrate clear relevance to the Ghanaian context.

## Challenge Timeline

*   **Deadline for application:** 1st July 2026
*   **Notifications - shortlisted teams:** 15th July 2026
*   **Summit Showcase:** Poster presentations, live pitches, and awards - 30th July 2026

## Submission Requirements

Three stages to showcase your work

Participants will submit deliverables in three stages:

#### 1 Technical Abstract

A 1–2 page document including:

*   • Problem statement and objectives
*   • Description of dataset(s) used and data sources
*   • Methodology and AI/ML techniques employed
*   • Preliminary results and key findings
*   • Potential impact and relevance to the problem area
*   • Team composition and relevant expertise

#### 2 Poster Presentation (Summit Day)

Shortlisted teams prepare a poster (A1 size recommended) covering:

*   • Visual summary of the solution
*   • Data processing and model architecture
*   • Results with key performance metrics
*   • Implementation pathway and scalability

#### 3 Live Pitch (Summit Day)

A 10–15 minute presentation to the judging panel including:

*   • Demonstration of the working solution
*   • Technical deep-dive on methodology
*   • Q&A session with judges (5–10 minutes)

