## Challenge Rules

Important guidelines to follow

*   Open to individuals or teams (maximum 5 members per team)
*   Participants must register before the development phase begins
*   Solutions must use at least one Ghanaian dataset as a primary data source
*   Datasets may be publicly available, self-collected, or obtained through partnerships (with appropriate permissions)
*   All data sources must be clearly documented and disclosed in the submission
*   Code must be submitted via a shared repository (e.g., GitHub) for reproducibility review
*   Participants retain intellectual property rights; organizers receive license to showcase work
*   All data handling must comply with ethical guidelines and data protection requirements
*   Decisions of the judging panel are final

## Team Formation & Diversity

Building stronger, more diverse teams

We strongly encourage diverse and collaborative team composition. Teams are encouraged to consider:

#### Gender Diversity

Mixed-gender teams are encouraged; teams with gender balance may receive recognition

#### Disciplinary Mix

Combining technical expertise with domain knowledge (e.g., agriculture, health, finance)

#### Experience Levels

Blending experienced professionals with students or early-career practitioners

#### Institutional Collaboration

Partnerships across academia, industry, government, and civil society

#### Geographic Representation

Including members from different regions of Ghana where possible

**Note:** Teams demonstrating exceptional diversity and collaboration may be considered for special recognition.

